Package: keyswitch
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCHITECTURE@
Maintainer: Oleg Shevchuk <sh.oleg@list.ru>
Depends: at-spi2-core, curl, libadwaita-1-0, libc6, libgcc-s1, libgtk-4-1, libxkbcommon0, libhunspell-1.7-0, hunspell-en-us, hunspell-ru
Homepage: https://github.com/olegius88/keyswitch
Description: automatic EN/RU keyboard layout correction for Ubuntu (X11 and Wayland)
 KeySwitch detects words entered using the wrong English or Russian keyboard
 layout, switches the active keyboard layout and replaces the already typed
 word on both X11 and Wayland desktops (GNOME Shell, KDE Plasma and sway). Its
 precision-first hybrid detector combines hard safety guards, frequency
 lexicons, Hunspell morphology, character n-grams, a checksum-validated bundled
 local linear classifier and explicit local rules. A separate local contextual
 classifier can keep, convert, wait or suggest using recent text. Optional
 AT-SPI field reading is disabled by default; no text is sent to a service.
 .
 It includes a GTK 4 and Libadwaita settings interface, global hotkeys,
 application and word exclusions, correction history, autostart integration
 and a desktop status indicator.
